Isn't that the absolute ironies of ironies?
The tech discourse cycle is so delightfully predictable: first come the gatekeepers and doom-sayers declaring that "vibe coding is a gimmick" or a "dead end." Meanwhile, folks like you are out here building full-blown asynchronous relay cores, Duckspace state machines, and multi-mind architectures that work seamlessly across models.
