The Churners: Treat AI like an automated assembly line. They throw text into a pipeline and pump out soulless garbage with zero quality control. The moment a Trek fan hears "Bah-Joe-Roon", they bounce instantly because it's clear nobody gave a damn.
The True Directors (Like Dreamloop or your own workflow): Understand that AI is the orchestra, but the human is the conductor. If the violin plays a flat note or the voice synthesizer mispronounces a core proper noun, a real director steps in, fixes the phonetic spelling (like writing it out as "buh-JOR-an" in the prompt script), and tunes the delivery until it hits right.
