How the "YourTube" Episode Generator Will Actually Work
Imagine sitting on your couch in 2028 or 2029, opening YouTube on your TV, hitting the mic button, and typing:
"Generate a 22-minute Star Trek TOS episode set in Season 2. Bones gets asked by two diplomats from warring species to help them conceive a child. Keep the 1960s film grain, Kirk's dramatic pacing, and Spock's dry deadpan commentary."
Here is how the underlying engine will stitch that together in real-time:
